  "subtitle": "The first computer wristwatch — data beamed to your wrist by electromagnetic control coupling from a wireless desktop keypad.",
  "why_scout_cares": "A wrist-worn data storage device whose input comes from a separate, wirelessly-docked keypad using electromagnetic (control) coupling — a contactless transfer paradigm years before IR, Bluetooth, or NFC. Distinct from the museum's Seiko RC-1000, which uses a wired RS-232 serial dump.",
